Greetings fellow dungeoneers,

I have created a standalone package for nethack 3.4.3 on Mac OS Lion,
with the X11 windowing system. I posted it at 
http://quatramaran.ens.fr/~coudert/NetHack_X11_MacOSLion.zip
in the hope that it is useful to others, and welcome feedback about it.
It contains a standalone Mac OS-style .app, which launches in X11.

X11 is an optional install on Mac OS Lion. You have the option of
installing the X11 package from your install media, or install the
community-provided XQuartz package (which I strongly recommend). The
NetHack package provided should work with both, but I have only tested it
under XQuartz.

Last noteworthy detail: this nethack build doesn't have permissions
control, so it will only run nice for the user who owns the app directory
(i.e. the user who downloaded it). If you want to have multiple users run
on the same system, go inside the app bundle and make the
Contents/Resources/nethackdir directory world-writable.

Happy hacking!

